ld deliver instantly. Every month regulators delay algorithmic deployment in credit markets, thousands of viable small business founders miss out on growth loans because human loan officers reject non-traditional credit profiles. Prohibiting software from making final hiring choices imposes a direct tax on labor mobility, trapping workers in legacy corporate structures where human managers dictate their wages. Congress enacted the Equal Credit Opportunity Act to expand access, not to enshrine manual bureaucratic gatekeeping as a moral virtue. Policymakers must dismantle these innovation barriers immediately to let decentralized software allocate capital and jobs without legacy interference.",
